{"title":"2025 BmMT Individual Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"border: 1px solid #444; background: #fff; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 20px auto; font-size: 90%; line-height: 1.6; font-family: sans-serif;\">\n<div style=\"background: #e0dbff; padding: 12px; text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid #444;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 110%; font-weight: bold; color: #4b3ba7;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_(Answer_Key)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual (Answer Key) (page does not exist)\">2025 BmMT Online Individual (Answer Key)</a></span><br />\n<span style=\"font-size: 95%; color: #6c5cb8;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Math_Tournament\" title=\"Berkeley Math Tournament\">BmMT Resources</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:Upload&amp;wpDestFile=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual.pdf\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual.pdf\">PDF</a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"padding: 15px 25px 15px 25px;\">\n<p style=\"font-weight: bold; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;\">Instructions</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 15px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">This test contains 20 short answer questions. All answers must be expressed in simplest form unless specified otherwise.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Each correct answer is worth 1 point. Each incorrect or blank answer is worth 0 points.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">No calculators are permitted. Protractors, rulers, and compasses are permitted.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">All answers should be written in the form of numbers only. When encountering ratios, express them using integers or fractions and do not use colon notation (e.g., use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> instead of 3:4).</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Do not include any units in your answers. Improper fractions and mixed numbers are both acceptable.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">You will have <b>60 minutes</b> working time to complete the test.</li>\n</ol>\n<div style=\"text-align: center; border-top: 1px solid #eee; padding-top: 12px; font-weight: bold; word-spacing: 2px;\">\n<p><a href=\"#Problem_1\">1</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_2\">2</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_3\">3</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_4\">4</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_5\">5</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_6\">6</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_7\">7</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_8\">8</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_9\">9</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_10\">10</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_11\">11</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_12\">12</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_13\">13</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_14\">14</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_15\">15</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_16\">16</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_17\">17</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_18\">18</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_19\">19</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_20\">20</a>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Timothe is reserving 100 classrooms for BmMT this year, and each room has exactly one purpose: testing, grading, or activities. Half of the rooms are for testing and four rooms are for grading. How many rooms are left for activities?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a straight line, not necessarily in that order. The distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is 15, and the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is 7. What is the sum of all distinct possible distances between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Benji writes down 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and Kiran writes down 6, 7, 8, 9, 10. Later, Kiran erases some of his numbers so that the sum of his remaining numbers equals the sum of Benji’s numbers. What is the sum of the numbers that Kiran erased?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bag contains two red marbles, two blue marbles, two green marbles, and two yellow marbles. Richard removes marbles from the bag one at a time without replacement. What is the least number of marbles Richard must remove to guarantee that two of the marbles that he has taken out are the same color?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four consecutive even integers sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f1588c7ab561762e3d7b81887b584140570fd01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-20$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. What is the product of these four integers?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are vertices shared by two congruent regular hexagons (shaded) and two equilateral triangles (unshaded) with the same side lengths. Together, these shapes form a larger, non-regular hexagon (drawn with a thick border). What is the ratio of the combined area of both regular hexagons (the shaded area) to the area of the large hexagon?\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive factors of 84 are divisible by 3? Note that 1 and 84 are positive factors of 84.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Luke the frog lives on a pond with 4 lilypads, labeled 1 through 4. He starts at lilypad 1 and, at every step, hops to a lilypad with a larger number, chosen uniformly at random. Luke continues hopping until he reaches lilypad 4. What is the probability that it takes Luke exactly 2 steps to reach lilypad 4?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Around equilateral triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and semicircles with diameters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are drawn. If the total area of the shaded region (the whole shape excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962dc703779ff99076fc817640ccaa24e92dae14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3300\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, what is the perimeter of parallelogram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />?\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Aaron has four coins. These coins have values of 1, 10, 100, and 1000 cents. Aaron makes a list of all the different numbers of cents he can make with some or all of his coins. If Aaron adds up all the numbers in his list, what is the result in cents?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a circle. Let segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> extend through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circle. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bf4c8fb259ed0881c6205dfd7055cea9e228932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff67bed50815f029660d4da83fcd8b16c9f9176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c577428f8c7d5deaaf8eefe8641b36af2b281d05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACD = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/1/661928fca01ec0ebba5f5d7bc026c3c0348f4270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - nx + 72 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" /> has two positive integer solutions, and one solution is an integer multiple of the other.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is two-cool if the decimal expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/77678819c52fdcf5763c1ec2e58107569767a277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n/250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"49\" height=\"20\" /> has exactly one or three digits past the decimal point, excluding trailing zeros. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/628e0d51d1f4f1a9e347a58a3e411a5ed32a5bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10/250 = 0.04$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> has exactly two digits past the decimal point, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5abb6691d47b2c20222bd1414582a52cc231f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100/250 = 0.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> has exactly one digit past the decimal point, so 100 is two-cool but 10 is not. How many positive integers less than 35 are two-cool?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define a sequence of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d745b81add053aa31f45d72cb9a898e3441e74bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b1171ce641826e9aca894162f9c15a57f6b46e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0cb860a94148254e4b58ac70c958bee9111a46a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i = 61a_{i-1} + i\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" />\nfor all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de27897c33d0e2c6dbad8cc49e06b972ad055958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />. What is the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896d56965b17443a55b2b5e55f798adf6465380d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> are divisible by 12?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed1661ca962f5807f3c0d27920cbed3f0b172ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c, d, e)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> be a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a841a89e2a1c16addd5b732f3542c1eae3be93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 3, 5, 7, 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />. For example, a possible permutation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7b59b7e8e846987dd936a4b71ba2523a0e2fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c, d, e) = (7, 3, 9, 1, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"20\" />. What is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbf685a01e893cedd92c9d85637e84dc4d94c21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a - ab + abc - abcd + abcde$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"221\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/a/c1ace926aaab1d20e0a81aa03e26679e6ece2b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab, abc, abcd,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/18396b1d04475fed55fd7c1b75cd4d85133210be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abcde$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> all represent multiplication?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nikki chooses three distinct square cells, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, from a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/457a92fa44ed3ac774c75cab0d841dba0d96c6a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 6$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> square grid uniformly at random. What is the probability that square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is contained within the rectangle whose opposite corners are squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />?\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f73d811eca6419d9c9a27423331d71ff06eb957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe954ed4e2115ef5fa939b7aa56362ced50d4ffa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a, b, c, 2025 \\cdot 6^7\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" /> is a geometric sequence that is strictly increasing, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8c4830d1666aa3cb4989aede3250c76066acda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b &lt; c &lt; 2025 \\cdot 6^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />. Find the number of distinct possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> be a regular hexagon. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e4f2d5cc59e5ffbed3734130e8c45b643adc91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and let line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036ee8c522d42dd4c4520b90f197a0ee97d379e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{CP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"21\" /> intersect segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164abb6bd18d06bfe942472fac852a1df64b2f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e7e50688ba04db04b5682a12ab18e5b456ce87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BP}{PF} = \\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"39\" />, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Danielle calculates the ones digit of each of the 2048 integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f58fa56a7e7a9cac1517ff76fb75dd102edaaab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{1!}, 2^{2!}, 3^{3!}, \\dots, 2048^{2048!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" />. If Danielle adds up all these ones digits, what is the resulting value?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There exist strictly increasing arithmetic sequences of real numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af56e439a2c6e0a48f8f7d071e008e58e734f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a, b, c\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625d4af821cbc18914d50946dee281b8105ea848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{p, q, r\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, having the properties that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a positive integer greater than 1 and that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/9/47972fd08d334ba9ca4ac239cef69eac38140bee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-ax^2+bx-c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" /> has solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec2b6f850a38c18bff9b2d860b248982102966e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Over all such pairs of increasing arithmetic sequences, what is the least possible value of the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/63795f5ae81b5558afc51ffd1b2e8a7a30d38f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Online_Individual_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 BmMT Online Individual Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:BmMT_Individual_box&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:BmMT Individual box (page does not exist)\">Template:BmMT Individual box</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tournament&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tournament (page does not exist)\">Berkeley Mini Math Tournament</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BmMT_Problems_and_Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"BmMT Problems and Solutions (page does not exist)\">BmMT Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions\">Mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203248\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.096 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 525/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 120/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13876/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.320      1 -total\n 16.09%    2.465      1 Template:BmMT_Individual_box\n 15.59%    2.389      3 Template:Missing_Diagram\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37780:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017203248 and revision id 292066. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}